# DATABASE_URL is the only variable this service reads.
#
# Copy this file to .env (which is gitignored) and set ONE of the lines
# below. This service keeps its own .env deliberately: fitting the model
# wants a fully ingested season, which during development means reading
# production, while apps/ingestion stays pointed at a local database.
# Repointing a shared .env to fit a model would also silently move where
# the ingestion pipeline WRITES.
#
# Local dev database (docker-compose.yml, see getting-started.md). Fine for
# running the service end to end; too little data for the fit to mean
# anything, since the archetype model needs a full season of games.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:55432/nba_analytics"

# Production, for fitting and inspecting the model against real data. Copy
# the commented production line from apps/api/.env. Scripts that only read
# open the connection with read_only=True, so the server itself rejects a
# write — pointing here to look at a fit is safe by construction.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project>:<password>@aws-0-eu-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# NOTE when copying a URL out of apps/api/.env: strip any "?schema=public"
# or "?pgbouncer=true". Those are Prisma options, not libpq ones, and libpq
# rejects the entire connection string on an unrecognised URI parameter.
# db.py strips both for you, so a verbatim copy works — but every other
# tool you might paste that URL into (psql, a GUI client) will not.
